  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts armed individuals in a combat setting, juxtaposed with text that reads 'just because your islamaphobic doesn't mean they don't want to kill you.' This combination is intended to provoke fear and reinforce harmful stereotypes by linking Islamophobia with violent intent. The visual of armed figures, often associated with terrorism, is used to amplify the message that those who hold Islamophobic views are perceived as being in danger from Muslims, which is a hateful and dangerous generalization. The meme uses the visual of armed individuals to symbolize the perceived threat from Muslims, thereby reinforcing the stereotype that Muslims are inherently violent and dangerous, which is a form of Islamophobic hate speech. The intent is to instill fear in the viewer and to promote a negative perception of Muslims by associating them with violence, which is a direct attack on a protected characteristic (religion).",
